mental model: i need to develop:

1. Do I have an interface?
        ↓
     ip a

2. Do I have the correct IP/subnet?
        ↓
     ip a

3. Do I have a route?
        ↓
     ip route

4. Which route will be used?
        ↓
     ip route get <destination>

5. Can I reach the destination?
        ↓
     ping <destination>

6. Is DNS resolving correctly?
        ↓
     dig <domain>

7. Is the destination port reachable?
        ↓
     nc -vz <host> <port>

8. Is my application listening?
        ↓
     ss -ltnp

9. Does the HTTP service actually respond?
        ↓
     curl -v <URL>

10. Where exactly are packets going?
        ↓
     traceroute / tcpdump



If you master:
-->     ip, ss, curl, dig, ping, nc, tcpdump, and ssh

you'll have a very strong practical command-line networking toolkit.




